From b047cf77998ebfee2439dc5f936e61b8d10ced56 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 22:18:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 09/10] Docs: drop a redundant explicit link target that failed
 `cargo doc`

onchain-runtime denies rustdoc warnings; `cargo doc --all-features
--no-deps` (the step after clippy in the upstream check job) rejected
`[ShieldedTokenType](coin_structure::coin::ShieldedTokenType)` because the
label already resolves to that item. The whole-workspace doc build passes
with the shorter form.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Q9CJgdhDhwqKR5eCeFM2VG
---
 onchain-runtime/src/context.rs | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/onchain-runtime/src/context.rs b/onchain-runtime/src/context.rs
index cd142902..563fc8fb 100644
--- a/onchain-runtime/src/context.rs
+++ b/onchain-runtime/src/context.rs
@@ -620,7 +620,7 @@ impl Distribution<ClaimedUnshieldedSpendsKey> for Standard {
 /// contract chose, together with the [`SpendRule`] the minted token type
 /// commits to. Together with the calling contract's address this fully
 /// determines the minted
-/// [`ShieldedTokenType`](coin_structure::coin::ShieldedTokenType).
+/// [`ShieldedTokenType`].
 #[derive(Clone, Debug, PartialEq, Eq, PartialOrd, Ord, Serializable, Storable, Hash)]
 #[storable(base)]
 #[tag = "contract-effects-shielded-mint-key[v1]"]
